  "finalReply": "Wrote `eval.scm`, a metacircular evaluator for the `interp.py` language.\n\nDesign:\n- Environments as lists of mutable frames (association lists), with `lookup`/`define-var!`/`set-var!` using `set-car!`/`set-cdr!` so closures and mutual recursion (including nested defines) work.\n- Compound procedures tagged `(procedure params body env)`; primitives tagged `(primitive name)` and dispatched in `apply-prim` by calling the host primitive directly, so `display`/`newline`/`read`/`getchr`/`putchr`/`chr`/`symbol` and all file ops (`fopen`/`fread`/`fgetchr`/`fputchr`/`fdisplay`/`fclose`) delegate to the host — stdin/stdout/file behavior is preserved through nesting.\n- Supports all special forms: `quote`, `if` (only `#f` is false, via host `not` identity check), `define` (both shapes), `set!`, `lambda` (incl. 0-arg thunks), `let`, `begin`/`progn`, `cond` with `else`, plus first-class primitives (so `(fold-left + ...)` works) and user shadowing of primitives.\n- Variadic `+`/`*`/`and`/`or` folded through binary host calls, preserving host semantics exactly.\n- Driver reads exactly one line with `(read)` as the guest filename, then loops `(fread fh)` + `mc-eval` until EOF.\n\nVerification performed:\n- All three spec commands produce `Reading / 15 / Done` for `(+ 7 8)`, including double self-hosting (`eval.scm` running `eval.scm` running `calculator.scm`).\n- Compared direct `python3 interp.py test/...` vs `printf 'test/...' | python3 interp.py eval.scm` for all 29 non-interactive tests — outputs identical.\n- Interactive tests match: `test_read.scm`, `calculator.scm` (`-`/`*` too), `06-interactive-io.scm`.",
